.TH AUTH-EVENT-SUMMARY 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
auth-event-summary \- summarize selected sudo, su and PAM message patterns privately
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B auth-event-summary
.RB [ --input " FILE|-" ]
.RB [ --null ]
.RB [ --help | --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Read finite, traditional RFC3164-like offline syslog data with optional
canonical PRI. Classify selected sudo/su/pam_unix log MESSAGE patterns
without outputting identities, commands, source paths or raw log text.
This is message counting, not verification of privileged activity,
successful command completion, login attempts or security incidents.
No implicit host-log access or writes; no authentication or network traffic.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --input " FILE|-"
Read regular file (reject symlinks), or stdin (default).
.TP
.B --null
Emit eleven rows with exactly two NUL-terminated fields each, no heading.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print usage.
.TP
.B --version
Print tool version.
.SH OUTPUT
TSV columns EVENT and COUNT. Classes SUDO_COMMAND, SUDO_DENIED, SU_SUCCESS,
SU_FAILED, PAM_AUTH_FAILURE, PAM_SESSION_OPEN, PAM_SESSION_CLOSE,
OTHER_AUTH, OTHER_SERVICE, UNKNOWN and TOTAL. One class per input line.
PAM sessions are not proof of password authentication; sudo COMMAND logs
are not proof of command success. User/IP/host/command/message are never shown.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Complete valid input, possibly including failure and OTHER events.
.TP
.B 1
Unrecognized envelope/PRI counted as UNKNOWN in otherwise complete input.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments.
.TP
.B 3
Input, framing, symlink or limits failure; no partial report.
.SH LIMITS
Maximum 16 MiB, 128 KiB per physical record, 50,000 records. Every nonempty
input must end in LF; CRLF allowed. No follow/rotation, RFC5424/ISO timestamp,
native macOS Unified Log or guaranteed complete authentication coverage.
Only sudo, sudo-i, su, su-l tags and matching pam_unix service families are
considered. Emitter-controlled messages are not forensic proof.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh-auth-summary (1),
.BR syslog-summary (1),
.BR journal-summary (1)
